{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1341110-blood-treachery","id":1341110,"title":"Blood Treachery","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-10-13T11:11:11-07:00","id":1341110,"title":"Blood Treachery","content":"I am seeking advice from my fellow gamers. Tomorrow night's game, my character and the other players are facing off against a gang of vampires. Last week left off on a cliff hanger. I am pretty confident that I can handle it. I *am* a Hermetic Magus after all <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. And I have a hunch the GM knows what I am going to do. The title of this thread, Blood Treachery, is an old M3 book I got used in great shape. I forget the name of the spell (I will print it out to bring to the game), but I intend to fill the room with sunlight. (90% certain the GM is expecting it, but there is a 10% doubt. As a long time GM myself, I have sympathy for the SG challenge of dealing with random ideas from players. I also try to bump the other players into the plot hat hand (beneficial metagaming). That is background info. Also, I am a Sorcerers Crusade mage, and the setting is New Jersey 1775.<br /> <br /> My question is not about tactics though. It is about strategy. If I do this, and I realize it will be as vulgar as fuck, I am pretty sure that I have to wipe out every single one so word doesn't get out that I cast spells like that one. More sticky points. I have been saddled with two apprentices that were given to me by an ancient vampire. One that is waaaay more powerful than I. I want to burn it, but I knew I had to parley. I am guessing he would be resistant to the sunlight spell? If not, clue me in. I know little about vampires.<br /> And these two apprentices, I guess the fiend has some lingering humanity, and wanted to remove these mortal children from the horror they faced for their future.Out of game, I know they are Revenants. In game it was hinted to me. I did not know what that meant, until I read about it in Blood Treachery. I need to keep my character from knowing what I know, or he will set them on fire.<br /> So, BIG question. Is there any way to cure them? Or at least, is it feasible for my character to *think* it is possible. Is setting them on fire the better option? Am I overreacting in sheer horror from what I read in Blood Treachery?<br /> As a side note, these two kids (actually adults but they look like they are 10), they are with my character in this scene. My plan is to use them as shield grogs to give me time to cast the spell. And, from what I read, they should be able to handle themselves. If they are to be *my* students, they need to learn that to be a Magus Flambeau, one must be both soldier and sorcerer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25651,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25651-marko-markoko","user":"Marko Markoko","date":".  typos and misspelling 10-13-2019, 02:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25651-marko-markoko","name":"Marko Markoko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25651_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-13T12:36:22-07:00","id":1341122,"title":"","content":"Can you give me a TL;DR version? That's a big wall of text that's kinda all over the place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-13T14:49:30-07:00","id":1341147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marko Markoko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1341110-blood-treachery#post1341110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, BIG question. Is there any way to cure them? Or at least, is it feasible for my character to *think* it is possible. Is setting them on fire the better option? Am I overreacting in sheer horror from what I read in Blood Treachery?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, sure there is a way to save them. This is the Age of Enlightenment and you are a powerful, insightful Mage, able to use their intellect to destroy these backwards looking creatures!What better sign that intellect and understanding are more powerful than simple physical, blood-bound fury? With the right instruction these children can be raised to overcome their base desires.<br /> <br /> OOC: No idea if you can stop them being Revenants or not within the rules of the game (probably, yes...?)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/133-guinbang","name":"guinbang","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-13T20:33:21-07:00","id":1341208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1341110-blood-treachery?p=1341122#post1341122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you give me a TL;DR version? That's a big wall of text that's kinda all over the place.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no idea what TL;DR means. But don't worry about it.Guinbang gave me an idea how to role play this situation out.<br /> <br /> HOWEVER, if you or anyone has knowledge of vampires, I would like to know more about how sunlight affects them. Are they able to develop some sort of resistance against it? How does the damage apply in mechanical terms?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25651-marko-markoko","name":"Marko Markoko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25651_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-13T22:32:55-07:00","id":1341219,"title":"","content":"Mechanically it has always been lackluster. Basically, sunlight hits a vampire and they take damage. They can soak it, but only with fortitude. The Soak difficulty varies based on how they are dressed. Basically naked is like DC 8 or 9, heavy clothing + sunscreen is like 6-7-8 (I forget which).<br /> <br /> The damage is rather lackluster but I don't think the damage is rolled, only soak is rolled. It's like 3 aggravated a turn. I know I said lackluster but in the lore a vampire hitting sunlight basically explodes and dies, while in practice if you are lucky and have some fortitude you can see the light of day and get away pretty easily.<br /> <br /> Resistance: Not that I'm aware of. There are some thaumaturgy rituals that may help and maybe high level fortitude. If you are a thinblood there is a merit (Atleast in V5) that the sunlight doesn't hurt you, but you can't do supernatural shit while in it and have half health.<br /> <br /> Damage in mechanical terms: They hit sunlight, their only hope is to have fortitude and soak. Barring that: They take like 3 aggravated, it may be a different number and it may vary by how much sunlight hits them. They also have to roll to resist fear frenzy.<br /> <br /> How does sunlight effect vampires: Unless thinblood + Merit, they explode. (Well, burn quickly). Vampires with 10 humanity (Atleast in V5) take half damage from sunlight. In V5 they also take damage equal to their blood potency, so they literally take more damage the stronger their blood is. Take that you cursed fucks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","name":"Jihelu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-14T05:01:56-07:00","id":1341237,"title":"","content":"Sunlight, like fire, is a powerful existential threat to a creature that doesn't fear much so you'd hope it would cause a panic response at least. This is called Rotschrek (The Red Fear) and according to V20 rules the Vampire flees in a blind panic from the source of their fear. The panic can be avoided with a Courage roll. Whether a panic response is useful to you, depends upon too much for me to comment on here...<br /> <br /> As a side note, do you know whether your ST is running the full Vampire the Masquerade rules? When I've ran cross-overs I've tended to keep to the spirit of the other splat's rules rather than their specific rulesets for various reasons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/133-guinbang","name":"guinbang","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-14T10:02:35-07:00","id":1341269,"title":"","content":"This is a full on oWoD mix. And (no judgment) he likes mixing in elements from the Buffy tVS games.<br /> I am the only one with M20 material (or any 20th material). He is a huuuuge Vampire fan. But there are no PC vamps (that I know of). I am the new guy in a circle that has been going for years. His wife plays a werebear, one guy is a Sorcerer, and the third, I don't even know, a mortal newspaperman (in 1775) with some power with printed/written word.There are NPC mages about. I am the only player mage, and I can tell he is happy that someone is playing one.<br /> <br /> So, best I can figure for an answer, he seems to be running rules as full as required for the elements present in the campaign at any given moment. It is a big bite, I know. I am running Sorcerers Crusade rules for my character (his suggestion), and I had to remind him about the Scourge/Fortune thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25651-marko-markoko","name":"Marko Markoko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25651_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-14T10:59:14-07:00","id":1341281,"title":"","content":"Sounds like a fun game! I think that fear of sunlight has been a thing through all the editions of VtM, so I would imagine he'll play it that way. If the Vampire does succumb to Rotschrek then it will want to flee in a panic, but that it will lash out in fury at anything in its way. I think it also gets to ignore any damage penalties due to health level damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/133-guinbang","name":"guinbang","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-20T17:27:57-07:00","id":1342609,"title":"","content":"as far as curing vampirism, I know that 'Red Sign' (a mage/Vampire crossover supplement) deals with that very fact. You might be able to look there for ideas on how to achieve the 'curing' goal. I also know that some of the subplots of Gehenna had Dhampirs weakening and becoming mortal as the curse 'faded.' Dhampir are functionally revenants so it stands to reason what works on the former works on the latter. It simply comes down to devising a means of weakening the curse (or simulating the withering. Again Red Sign may come in handy for that.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-22T02:49:10-07:00","id":1342907,"title":"","content":"I will look that book up. I mentioned that at the game tonight and the gm suggested I look into it.<br /> Oh! That spell I mentioned. Glorious Sword of Heaven. Rolled very well and I turned a gang of fledgling vampires to ash right off the bat at the start of game. Also rolled well for Initiative, so that helped. After many years of just running games, it is fun and exciting to be a player for a change. Ah, The thrill of the random dice roll...<br /> Now keep in mind, I know very little about Vampires in oWoD. Or any vampire game. I was unsure about how much damage would be inflicted, if vampires can resist sunlight, nada. And that adds to the fun. My character has a score of 3 in Vampire Lore, so he is familiar with the (slanted) lore contained in Blood Treachery. And as a <i>player</i>, most of my actual knowledge comes straight from Blood Treachery, and vague memories of playing V2 around twenty years ago.Itis nice to be reminded that a little mystery is fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25651-marko-markoko","name":"Marko Markoko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25651_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-22T04:06:42-07:00","id":1342912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marko Markoko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1341110-blood-treachery?p=1342907#post1342907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Itis nice to be reminded that a little mystery is fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>OWoD in general has the problem that the books and fluff try to categorize and explain every little mystery and mechanic - and after all these years, of course most players know all that stuff, so suprising them can be damn hard. They don't see a creepy vampire creature, they see a &quot;Gangrel, probably neonate, and oh look there's his claws, we were right&quot;.<br /> <br /> Personally I think the OWoD is much larger and mysterious than just what's written in the books, and I always encourage STs to create things that don't fit the norm. (Don't get me started on 'if it's not explained, it's a spirit'....)<br /> All the creepy crawlies and spooky horrors and eldritch things. Because even the splats of the WoD don't necessarily know what's out there.<br /> It is, really, one of the advantages of CoD - it all feels much more lovecraftian and mysterious in parts. Heck, the entire principle of the God-Machine along with the abstract concept of its servants is, in my mind, amazeballs.<br /> But I believe good OWoD stories can go there. All it needs is a bit of creativity and not sticking 100% to past books and metaplot &quot;Because established fluff.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 10-22-2019, 07:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-22T13:40:23-07:00","id":1343004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1341110-blood-treachery?p=1342912#post1342912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OWoD in general has the problem that the books and fluff try to categorize and explain every little mystery and mechanic - and after all these years, of course most players know all that stuff, so suprising them can be damn hard.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does seem to me, that they are currently willing to re-write anything changing it as they move forward. Maybe we will see some suprises from that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}